  "query_preview": "..\nBelow to much below average temperatures will continue through \ntonight, with a gradual warming trend bringing more moderate \ntemperatures thereafter. Upper ridging begins building late \nThursday night following a strengthening low off the coast of Baja\nCalifornia. As the ridge tracks east, highs trend back above \naverage for the weekend. Highs look to peak on Saturday with mid\nto upper 70s.\n\nDry weather will continue through the week, save for the potential\nfor patchy fog overnight tonight. The next chance for precip looks\nto be mid week next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\nLowered day 1 and 2 temperatures to further collaboration\nfollowing NBM10 guidance. Wednesday temperatures are a bit more \nuncertain, following subtle ridging over central and eastern MT, \ncaused by the track of the low over the intermountain west. \nRegardless, the uncertainty remains non impactful. \n\nLow confidence in patchy fog this morning.",
